  <!-- T20 Section -->
  <h2 id="two">India T20 Cricket</h2>
  <p>
    A Twenty20 International (T20I) is a form of cricket match between two representative teams,
    each having T20I status as determined by the International Cricket Council (ICC).
    The first such match was played between Australia and New Zealand on 17 February 2005.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Indian cricket team played its first T20I match under the captaincy of Virender Sehwag during the 2006–07 series in South Africa.
    India defeated the hosts by six wickets in the one-off match.
  </p>
  <p>
    India won the inaugural ICC World Twenty20, defeating Pakistan in the final by five runs.
  </p>

